# Always Use Braces

Every control-flow body must use `{ }`, even when it is a single statement. Do not omit braces.

Applies to: `if`, `else`, `for`, `while`, `do-while`.

```java
// ❌ BAD
if (condition)
    doSomething();
if (x > 0) return false;
for (Unit u : units) process(u);

// ✅ GOOD
if (condition) {
    doSomething();
}
if (x > 0) {
    return false;
}
for (Unit u : units) {
    process(u);
}
```

```java
// ❌ BAD
if (a) foo();
else bar();

// ✅ GOOD
if (a) {
    foo();
} else {
    bar();
}
```

When editing existing code, add braces to any control-flow body you touch that omits them.